MSG_DISKSFULL_TXT (//)
All four file disks are in use.\nClear one on the Volumes tab first.
;
MSG_CHK_MISSING_TXT (//)
File disk %ld is not there:\n%s\n\nThe Mac would start without it.
;
MSG_CHK_MISSING_GADS (//)
Settings|Start anyway|Quit
;
MSG_CHK_ROMCHIP_TXT (//)
The ROM is set to "24 bit DMA" memory, but this\nAmiga has no 24-bit fast RAM, so the ROM would take\na megabyte of chip RAM. 256-colour screens then\ncome out white.\n\nUse "Any" memory for the ROM this time?\n(Change it on the Memory tab and Save to keep it.)
;
MSG_CHK_ROMCHIP_GADS (//)
Use Any|Start anyway|Settings|Quit
;
MSG_CHK_COPYBACK_TXT (//)
This is a 68060 in UAE, and NOCOPYBACK is off.\nWithout it the Mac usually stops on a grey screen.\n\nTurn NOCOPYBACK on this time?\n(Tick it on the CPU tab and Save to keep it.)
;
MSG_CHK_COPYBACK_GADS (//)
Turn it on|Start anyway|Settings|Quit
;
MSG_APPICON_NAME (//)
Mac disk
;
MSG_PRISM15_TXT (//)
PrismRTG has this screen size in 15 bit too. The Mac\ndraws straight into a 15-bit screen; this 16-bit\nscreen has to be converted, which is slower.\n\nUse the 15-bit mode?
;
MSG_PRISM15_GADS (//)
Use 15 bit|Keep 16 bit
;
MSG_PRISM15OFF_TXT (//)
This 16-bit screen has to be converted, which is slower.\nPrismRTG can offer 15-bit modes, which the Mac draws\ninto directly. Turn them on in the PrismRTG prefs\n(for example MODE=640x480x15 ON) and restart Prism.
;
MSG_SETUP_WELCOME_TXT (//)
Welcome to ShapeShifter!\n\nThere are no settings yet. ShapeShifter can set itself\nup for this Amiga: find the Mac ROM, choose the screen,\nmemory and CPU options, and create an empty Mac disk\nto install the Mac system on. You can change all of it\nin the settings window afterwards.
;
MSG_SETUP_WELCOME_GADS (//)
Set up|Skip
;
MSG_SETUP_ROMFOUND_TXT (//)
ShapeShifter needs a Mac ROM image in\nPROGDIR:ShapeShifter ROM. This file looks like one:\n\n%s (%ldK)\n\nCopy it there?
;
MSG_SETUP_ROMFOUND_GADS (//)
Copy it|Choose another...|Skip
;
MSG_SETUP_NOROM_TXT (//)
ShapeShifter needs a Mac ROM image (512K or 1MB,\nfrom a 68020 to 68040 Mac) in PROGDIR:ShapeShifter ROM.\n\nChoose the ROM file to copy there?
;
MSG_SETUP_NOROM_GADS (//)
Choose...|Skip
;
MSG_SETUP_ROMHAIL (//)
Choose the Mac ROM file
;
MSG_SETUP_BADROM_TXT (//)
%s is not a Mac ROM image\n(it must be 512K or 1MB).
;
MSG_SETUP_COPYFAIL_TXT (//)
The ROM could not be copied to\nPROGDIR:ShapeShifter ROM.
;
MSG_SETUP_DISK_TXT (//)
Create an empty %ld MB Mac disk to install the\nMac system on?\n\n%s\n\nIt becomes File disk 1, an empty Mac disk named "Mac disk":\ninstall the system on it from its CD.
;
MSG_SETUP_DISK_GADS (//)
Create|No
;
MSG_SETUP_DISKFAIL_TXT (//)
The Mac disk could not be created\n(not enough room?):\n%s
;
MSG_SETUP_DONE_TXT (//)
ShapeShifter has chosen:\n\nScreen: %s\nMemory for the Mac: %ld MB\n%s\nCheck the settings window and click Save to keep them.
;
MSG_SETUP_SCR_CGX (//)
graphics card, 640x480, 256 colours
;
MSG_SETUP_SCR_AGA (//)
AGA screen, 256 colours
;
MSG_SETUP_SCR_BW (//)
Amiga screen, black and white
;
MSG_SETUP_NOCB (//)
NOCOPYBACK is on (68060 in UAE).\n
;
MSG_CPUOPT8_GAD (//)
Mac chooses the colour depth (DEPTHSWITCH)
;
;
; Gadget help (window title line)
;
MSG_HELP_START (3000//)
Start the Mac with these settings
;
MSG_HELP_EXIT (//)
Quit ShapeShifter without saving
;
MSG_HELP_SAVE (//)
Save the settings in ShapeShifter Prefs
;
MSG_HELP_NUMMON (//)
One or two monitors; the right half is the second one
;
MSG_HELP_DEPTH (//)
Mac colours; more colours on Amiga screens is slower
;
MSG_HELP_TYPE (//)
Amiga screen, graphics card (CyberGfx/P96), EGS, window
;
MSG_HELP_EXTVID (//)
Path of the external video driver (screen type External)
;
MSG_HELP_MODE (//)
Amiga screen mode for the Mac screen
;
MSG_HELP_SIZE (//)
Mac screen size in pixels; smaller is faster
;
MSG_HELP_REFRATE (//)
1/50 s between screen updates; higher leaves more CPU
;
MSG_HELP_BLACK (//)
Black border around the Mac screen, as on a real Mac
;
MSG_HELP_REFALWAYS (//)
Convert in 8 bit too, so the Mac never draws on another screen
;
MSG_HELP_MMUREF (//)
68040/060: only update the parts of the screen that changed
;
MSG_HELP_AMIMOUSE (//)
Use the Amiga mouse pointer on the Mac side as well
;
MSG_HELP_AFD (//)
Disk image: .hfv, DiskCopy floppy, CD image (Toast, .bin/.cue)
;
MSG_HELP_GETAFD (//)
Choose a disk image file
;
MSG_HELP_MAKEAFD (//)
Create a new empty disk image of a given size
;
MSG_HELP_ADD (//)
Amiga device of a Mac partition (e.g. scsi.device)
;
MSG_HELP_GETADD (//)
Choose a Mac partition; the values are filled in
;
MSG_HELP_ADDUNIT (//)
Unit of the device; for SCSI, the SCSI ID
;
MSG_HELP_ADDSECT (//)
Part of the disk the Mac may use; wrong values destroy data
;
MSG_HELP_MAXTRANS (//)
Largest transfer; as MaxTransfer in the mountlist (-1: none)
;
MSG_HELP_REMOV (//)
Notice media changes (SyQuest, ZIP, CD)
;
MSG_HELP_BOOT (//)
Which disk the Mac starts from
;
MSG_HELP_FLOPPY (//)
Amiga floppy drive used as this Mac floppy drive
;
MSG_HELP_SEARCH (//)
Find the first two floppy drives
;
MSG_HELP_INHIBIT (//)
Keep AmigaDOS off this drive while the Mac runs
;
MSG_HELP_SCSION (//)
Let the Mac use this SCSI ID
;
MSG_HELP_SCSIDRV (//)
Amiga SCSI driver for this ID (e.g. scsi.device)
;
MSG_HELP_SCSIUNIT (//)
Unit number for this ID, normally the SCSI ID
;
MSG_HELP_SCSIMEM (//)
Memory for SCSI buffers; 24 bit DMA for Zorro II DMA cards
;
MSG_HELP_APPLECD (//)
ShapeShifter's own CD-ROM driver for SCSI CD drives
;
MSG_HELP_APPLEHD (//)
Make Apple's HD SC Setup see an Apple hard disk
;
MSG_HELP_DIRECT (//)
SCSI transfers without a buffer, where the driver allows it
;
MSG_HELP_SUMMER (//)
Workaround for a bug in phase5 SCSI drivers
;
MSG_HELP_MEMSIZE (//)
Memory for the Mac in KB (ROM and screen need more)
;
MSG_HELP_MEMMAX (//)
Most memory the Mac can get now
;
MSG_HELP_LARGEST (//)
Give the Mac the largest free memory block
;
MSG_HELP_FASTROM (//)
Allocate the ROM first, so it gets the fastest memory
;
MSG_HELP_ROMMEM (//)
Memory for the ROM; Any unless a card needs 24 bit DMA
;
MSG_HELP_SERDRV (//)
Amiga driver for this Mac port (serial.device...)
;
MSG_HELP_SERUNIT (//)
Unit of the driver (0 for the built-in port)
;
MSG_HELP_SERPAR (//)
Tick if the driver is a parallel.device type
;
MSG_HELP_AMAX (//)
Use the ports of an A-Max/Emplant card instead
;
MSG_HELP_SANA (//)
SANA-II Ethernet driver (e.g. DEVS:Networks/...device)
;
MSG_HELP_SANAUNIT (//)
Unit of the network card, normally 0
;
MSG_HELP_MOUSE (//)
Read the mouse directly (more compatible, no tablets)
;
MSG_HELP_PROTROM (//)
68040: write-protect the Mac ROM with the MMU
;
MSG_HELP_MACOS8 (//)
Report a Quadra 900; needed for Mac OS 8, off for old Systems
;
MSG_HELP_AUDIO (//)
Mac sound output on or off
;
MSG_HELP_AHI (//)
Play Mac sound through AHI instead of the Amiga hardware
;
MSG_HELP_AHIMODE (//)
AHI audio mode for the Mac sound
;
MSG_HELP_CPUINFO (//)
The processor ShapeShifter found
;
MSG_HELP_NOCB (//)
Copyback cache off; a 68060 in UAE needs this
;
MSG_HELP_REMAP (//)
Put the Mac's low 8K into cacheable fast RAM (MMU)
;
MSG_HELP_ENFORCER (//)
Let Enforcer run at the same time (MMU)
;
MSG_HELP_MACTCP (//)
MacTCP through the Amiga's TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket)
;
MSG_HELP_USKEY (//)
Swap two keys so the `/~ key works on US keyboards
;
MSG_HELP_NOQD (//)
Turn ShapeShifter's drawing speedups off
;
MSG_HELP_720K (//)
Format 720K floppies under System 7.5 and later
;
MSG_HELP_DEBUG (//)
For debugging ShapeShifter itself; leave it off
;
MSG_HELP_DEPTHSW (//)
Change the colour depth in Monitors on the Mac (always copies the screen)
;
MSG_REPLACE_TXT (//)
%s\nis already there. Replace it with a new, empty disk?
;
MSG_REPLACE_GADS (//)
Replace|Cancel
;
MSG_BADPREFS_TXT (//)
%s\nis not a ShapeShifter settings file. The settings were not changed.
;
MSG_SAVEFAIL_TXT (//)
%s\ncould not be saved.
;
MSG_CHK_ADD4GB_TXT (//)
Device disk %ld lies beyond the first 4 GB of its drive.\nShapeShifter cannot reach it there.\n\nThe Mac would start without it.
;
MSG_PATHLONG_TXT (//)
%s\nis too long: at most %ld characters fit here.\nUse a shorter path or an Assign.
;
MSG_SETUP_MMUREF (//)
MMU refresh is on (only changed parts of the screen are redrawn).\n
;
MSG_CHK_SLOWSEEK_TXT (//)
File disk %ld is on a drive where jumping around in a\nlarge file is slow:\n%s\n\nA jump of 100 MB takes about %ld seconds there, and the Mac\nmakes thousands of jumps while it starts: it would start\nvery slowly and look as if it had stopped.\n\nIt is the Fast File System on a slow drive. Keep the image\non a PFS3 or SFS partition, or on a faster drive.
;
MSG_FORMATADD_GAD (//)
Format...
;
MSG_HELP_FORMATADD (//)
Write an empty Mac disk to this device disk, instead of letting the Mac initialise it
;
MSG_FMT_ASK_TXT (//)
Write an empty Mac disk to\n%s, unit %ld, from sector %ld (%ld MB)?\n\nEverything stored there now will be lost.
;
MSG_FMT_ASK_GADS (//)
Format|Cancel
;
MSG_FMT_DONE_TXT (//)
The Mac disk is ready: %ld MB, named "Untitled".\nThe Mac will show it at its next start.
;
MSG_FMT_NAME_TXT (//)
Enter the device and unit of the device disk first,\nor pick a partition with "Choose...".
;
MSG_FMT_NODEV_TXT (//)
%s, unit %ld could not be opened.\nNothing was written.
;
MSG_FMT_SIZE_TXT (//)
%s, unit %ld, from sector %ld:\nthis cannot become a Mac disk. It has to lie within the drive\nand its first 4 GB, be at least 1 MB large, and the drive\nhas to have sectors of 512 bytes.\n\nNothing was written.
;
MSG_FMT_RDB_TXT (//)
%s, unit %ld has an Amiga partition table.\nFormatting from sector %ld would destroy every partition\non the drive.\n\nNothing was written. Pick a partition with "Choose...".
;
MSG_FMT_WRERR_TXT (//)
Writing to %s, unit %ld failed.\nThe Mac disk there is incomplete.
MSG_DEFAULTS_GAD (//)
Defaults
;
MSG_DEFAULTS_DONE_TXT (//)
Suggested for this Amiga:\n\nScreen: %s\nMemory for the Mac: %ld MB\n%s\nDisks, ROM and devices are as they were.\nClick Save to keep the settings.
;
MSG_CHK_NODISK_TXT (//)
No Mac disk is set: no file disk, no device disk\nand no SCSI device.\n\nThe Mac would show a disk with a question mark\nand wait for a floppy disk.\n\nSet a disk on the "Volumes/Disks" tab.
;
MSG_CHK_LOWMEM_TXT (//)
The Mac gets only %ld KB of memory.\nSystem 7 needs about 8 MB and Mac OS 8 about 16 MB\nto work well.\n\nSet "Mac memory" on the "Memory" tab, or click\n"Defaults" in the settings window.
;
MSG_CHK_BADMODE_TXT (//)
The screen mode in the settings does not exist\non this Amiga (any more).\n\nChoose a screen mode on the "Graphics" tab,\nor click "Defaults" in the settings window.
;
MSG_CHK_BADMODE_GADS (//)
Settings|Quit
;
MSG_ADVANCED_GAD (//)
Advanced
;
MSG_SETUP_NOFILE_TXT (//)
The settings file\n%s\nis not there.\n\nShapeShifter starts with settings that fit this Amiga.\nNo disks are set.
;
